# Fleet core — every session

- Merge commits only: after every merge, `git log -1 --format=%p <sha>` shows two parents (#1743
  was a squash). Standing authority is AGENTS.md §Concurrent PRs: an orchestrator merges its own
  fleet's PRs (and lent ones) when `node tools/ci/merge-gate.mjs --pr <n>` exits 0 (the hook
  requires that receipt, pinned to the gated head). Nobody re-asks it at a hand-off; a `.claude/**`
  edit or a lifted hold is typed in the acting session.
- Orchestrators merge in parallel, each its own PRs; no lease gates a merge. A game PR takes the bus
  `GAME-SLOT` first and waits for green Pages on the last game merge; non-game PRs batch. `DONE` via
  bus; peer READY/HANDOFF/INCIDENT/INFO/QUESTION/REQUEST via `agent-msg.mjs`; read on bus wakes +
  hourly (#3773). A and B (two accounts) wake via the cross-account inbox (to the bus; 60 s watch). No authority.
- READY via `agent-msg.mjs` to your fleet's orchestrator; no Merge Desk unless Bryce designates one.
  Archive by `node tools/ci/fleet-archive.mjs <saved list_sessions page>` (a retired orchestrator
  too); never a session Bryce opened, a watcher or a live orchestrator. By hand only after
  `fleet-archive.mjs --hand <branch>` exits 0.
- The only veto is a PR-body line starting `MERGE-HOLD:`, never "do not merge" wording. On
  in-session rejection or "wait": put `MERGE-HOLD:` on the PR at once and tell the orchestrator.
  "wait" pauses this session (not the fleet): PR, ready, merge; still commit and push WIP.
- Draft→ready only when the tip is green and `node tools/ci/ready-gate.mjs --pr <n>` exits 0.
- Sync only when GitHub reports CONFLICTING/DIRTY or a required tip check is red
  (`needs-sync.mjs`); never for clean-behind. Merge origin, never force or rebase.
- After every push: subscribe (host tool), at most one `ci-watch --once`, then end the turn — never
  poll in a shell loop.
- Times in Pacific (`America/Los_Angeles`). Bryce plays on a phone: reproduce HUD/UI reports at
  844×390 landscape with touch first, not desktop.
